// Config for markdownlint (the VS Code extension and markdownlint-cli2 both
// read this file). Without it, the default ruleset reports ~900 "issues"
// across docs/, ~95% of them from two purely cosmetic rules the docs have
// never followed — enough noise to bury the handful that actually matter.
//
// Only rules deliberately turned off are listed; everything else stays at
// its default. Add a line here with its reason rather than reformatting a
// document to satisfy a rule nobody agreed to.
{
  // Line length (default 80). The docs are prose-first and hard-wrapped by
  // hand at whatever width reads well, and the reference documents (4.2,
  // 4.3, 4.5) carry wide tables whose cells cannot wrap at all. Enforcing a
  // column limit would reformat nearly every file to no benefit: it changes
  // nothing about how GitHub renders them.
  "MD013": false,

  // Table pipe spacing — wants `| a | b |` where these docs write `|a|b|`.
  // Cosmetic only, invisible once rendered, and 253 occurrences deep.
  "MD060": false
}
